● Here's a summary of what I found and fixed:
Root cause: Keystatic allows clicking "Add" in the Photos list without selecting a file. This writes photos: [{}] to the YAML — an empty object with no src key. The page check photos.length > 0 was truthy, so the photos section rendered, but photo.src was undefined → cdnUrl(undefined) → null → <img> with
no src attribute → invisible image.
Two fixes applied:
1. app/[locale]/about/page.tsx — added a validPhotos filter that drops any photo entry without a src before rendering. The section is now hidden when all entries are empty:
const validPhotos = photos?.filter(p => p.src) ?? []
2. content/about/de.mdx — removed the stale - {} entry (left from Keystatic saving without a file uploaded), back to photos: [].
How to add photos correctly: In Keystatic → About — DE → Photos → "Add" → choose a file first, then click "Add". The image uploads to public/about/ and the path is written to the YAML.

================================================================================
ATTEMPT 2 — 2026-05-05 — actual root cause and fix
================================================================================

Attempt 1 was wrong. It chased a side-issue (empty `{}` entries in the `photos`
array) but never addressed what the user actually saw missing: the **portrait
image**. The portrait file was on disk at `public/about/portrait/src.webp`, the
path `/about/portrait/src.webp` was correctly written to all three
`content/about/<locale>.mdx` files, R2 was serving the file at HTTP 200 — yet
nothing rendered on the page.

Root cause:
  app/[locale]/about/page.tsx never rendered the portrait at all. The component
  destructured `{ milestones, lineage, marginalia, photos }` from frontmatter
  but omitted `portrait`, and the JSX had no <img>/cdnUrl call for it. Bug
  present since the original cb0aaab "C5: about page" commit. The portrait
  field was loaded into memory by `loadAbout()` and silently dropped on render.

How attempt 1 missed it:
  Got distracted by the empty `photos: []` array and went deep on a Keystatic
  edge case (saving a photo item with no file → writes `- {}` to YAML). That's
  a real but minor bug; it doesn't explain why the portrait — which has a
  valid src and a real file behind it — wasn't showing. Should have first
  asked: "is any image rendering at all on this page?"

Fix applied (commit pending):
  1. app/[locale]/about/page.tsx
     - Added `portrait` to the frontmatter destructure (line 196).
     - Computed `portraitUrl = cdnUrl(portrait?.src)`.
     - Added a <figure className={styles.portrait}> block between the heading
       and the bio, with <img> + optional <figcaption> for the credit. Only
       renders when `portraitUrl` is truthy.

  2. app/[locale]/about/page.module.css
     - Added `.portrait` (max-width: --max-width-prose, margin-bottom: --space-7)
     - Added `.portraitImg` (display: block, width: 100%, height: auto)
     - Added `.portraitCredit` (mono, --font-size-meta, --ink-faint)

Verification:
  - curl https://pub-...r2.dev/about/portrait/src.webp → HTTP 200, 37562 bytes
    (matches local file size — R2 sync is healthy)
  - en.mdx, de.mdx, ru.mdx all carry the same /about/portrait/src.webp path
  - cdnUrl() correctly produces the R2 URL for that path

Note about the `validPhotos` filter from attempt 1:
  Kept as-is. It's still a correct guard against Keystatic's `- {}` artifact
  for the `photos` array (the gallery, not the portrait), even if it wasn't
  the bug the user was actually reporting.

Lesson:
  When the user says "no photo on the page", verify *which* photo. The about
  page has two image fields (portrait + photos array) and they are wired
  through completely independent code paths. Confirm the symptom (which DOM
  node is missing or broken) before theorizing about the data flow.
